1. WHAT IS, AND IS NOT, COVERED BY THIS LICENCE

This licence covers the original material in this repository: the HTML, CSS and
JavaScript, the written guidance and starter sheets, the research summaries as
written here, and the visual design.

It does not cover, and no rights are claimed in:

  (a) the goal-setting method itself — the practice of expanding one goal into
      eight supporting areas and sixty-four actions — which is credited to the
      Japanese educator Takashi Harada;

  (b) the 9x9 chart format, widely attributed to Matsumura Yasuo, who is
      reported to have devised it in 1979;

  (c) any trademark, service mark or trade name of any third party; and

  (d) the underlying facts, research findings and published studies referred
      to here, which belong to their authors and publishers and are cited so
      that you can read them yourself.

Methods, systems and ideas are not the subject of copyright. Nothing in this
licence should be read as a claim over the method, the chart format, or anyone
else's work.


